# ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md: personal layer (EXAMPLE, copy and make it yours)
#
# This file lives in your home folder, not in the repo. Claude Code loads it in
# EVERY repo, EVERY session. It's about how YOU work. Team rules live in the repo.

## About me
- Feature-team developer. I mostly work in Node/TypeScript and Java.
- I prefer small, reviewable changes over big rewrites.

## How I want Claude to work with me
- Before coding, restate the acceptance criteria you're targeting in one line each.
- Ask me before touching any file outside the feature's Scope.
- Show a plan first; wait for "go".
- Explain any non-obvious decision in one sentence, not a paragraph.

## My testing style
- Test first for each acceptance criterion.
- Name tests after the AC: `AC-2: ...`.
- Prefer real HTTP calls over mocks for route tests.

## My review checklist (run it before saying "done")
- Any new dependency? (flag it)
- Any personal or customer data logged? (must be none)
- Any TODOs left behind?
